{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>והעברת.</b> וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ is nothing but a term of separation, and so it says ״וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ אֶת נַחֲלָתוֹ לְבִתּוֹ״ (Numbers 27). (Mekhilta)" "<b>Every issue of a beast.</b> A stillborn that its mother cast forth and sent out before its time. Scripture teaches you that it is holy in its firstborn status to exempt the one born after it — even though a stillborn is not called שֶׁגֶר, as in ״שְׁגַר אֲלָפֶיךָ״ (Deuteronomy 7); rather, this comes only to teach about the stillborn, for it has already written כָּל פֶּטֶר רֶחֶם. And if you say: even the firstborn of an unclean beast is included in the meaning? It comes and specifies in another place ״בִּבְקָרְךָ וּבְצֹאנְךָ״ (Deuteronomy 15). Another interpretation: ״וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ כָל פֶּטֶר רֶחֶם״ — concerning the firstborn of man Scripture speaks."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:58.896945900Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}